ULL ACLI pattern it otherwise mirrors).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Landed _convert passes input=markdown to subprocess.run (wiki_render.py:330-336)","Cited ACLI pattern spawns with stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL (acli_subprocess.py:449) — acli takes no stdin, unlike pandoc","Plan writes only 'enforces the wall clock caller-side via proc.communicate(timeout=dc_pandoc_timeout_s)' with no input=/stdin=PIPE"],"finding":"The Approach specifies proc.communicate(timeout=dc_pandoc_timeout_s) but omits how the markdown reaches pandoc's stdin; the current _convert feeds it via subprocess.run(input=markdown), and pandoc reads from stdin, so the new Popen must set stdin=subprocess.PIPE and call communicate(input=markdown, timeout=...). The explicitly-cited ACLI pattern uses stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL because acli takes no stdin, so an implementer mirroring it verbatim would feed pandoc empty input and silently change output.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0d49e6166bac34f4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Hard timeout + process-group reaping'; wiki_render.py:325-343 (_convert)","norm_id":"ndb346ce58e73f7e5","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["Implementer copies the ACLI Popen kwargs verbatim (stdin=DEVNULL), pandoc gets empty stdin, every unit falls back — silently breaking the byte-identical-output AC"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add to the Approach: build the Popen with stdin=subprocess.PIPE, stdout/stderr=PIPE, text=True, and deliver the unit via proc.communicate(input=substitute_arrows(text), timeout=dc_pandoc_timeout_s) — matching _convert's existing input= semantics, not the ACLI stdin=DEVNULL case.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked