,"finding":"Batching a maximal run of contiguous _RENDER units into ONE pandoc commonmark document is not semantically equivalent to the landed per-unit rendering: pandoc parses block boundaries relative to surrounding content, so adjacent blocks (even separated by re-emitted blank lines) can reparse differently than in isolation (lazy paragraph continuation, setext-header underlines, reference-link definitions, list continuation). The plan's safety net — the run-level preservation check lifted from _render_unit — only verifies code_fragments survive (wiki_render.py:376-390, 266-288); it cannot detect prose-level cross-block reflow/merge, so batching can silently corrupt prose that the landed one-document-per-block design structurally prevented.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9ebc43ab185c5415","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Batch contiguous SAFE units to bound subprocess cost' / 'run-level preservation check'","norm_id":"n8aa1f3aa86e1f1cb","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"no","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The timeout AC's proving test test_dc_pandoc_timeout_falls_back 'asserts the group is reaped', but the plan does not specify that its fixture actually spawns a pipe-holding GRANDCHILD — the exact case (bpo-30154 / bug d843) that distinguishes reap_process_group from a plain subprocess.run(timeout=). A fixture whose pandoc stand-in only stalls the direct child would pass the assertion without ever exercising the killpg path the AC exists to prove.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1893a5161800ed07","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, line 1 (test_dc_pandoc_timeout_falls_back)","norm_id":"n7b2c7b880f10e8a9","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Have the timeout fixture invoke a stand-in that double-forks / spawns a sleeping grandchild holding the stdout pipe, capture its PID, and assert os.kill(grandchild_pid, 0) raises ProcessLookupError after fallback.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy",